CVE-2026-34260 needs authentication: it is an SQL injection through user-controlled input in S/4HANA's Enterprise Search for ABAP ([EUVD-2026-29371](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-29371)), and because the affected code only reads data its integrity impact is none, so the reach is database reads and availability rather than full read and write ([Onapsis, 2026-05-12](https://onapsis.com/blog/sap-security-patch-day-may-2026/)). CVE-2026-34263 in Commerce Cloud needs no authentication but SAP's vector requires user interaction ([SAP, May 2026](https://support.sap.com/en/my-support/knowledge-base/security-notes-news/may-2026.html)), and its root cause is improper Spring Security configuration ([EUVD-2026-29372](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-29372)). HotNews Note 3747787 for the SAP Cloud Application Programming npm compromise was released on 2026-04-30 ([Onapsis, 2026-05-12](https://onapsis.com/blog/sap-security-patch-day-may-2026/)), and none of the cited sources links either product to Swiss federal programmes or says how often Commerce Cloud deployments face the internet.
